{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtqtniQ66wE3rNWwKZw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The phrase counts argue against a pure \"closes too late\" story. Finished ×2 samples almost always pass through an explicit wrap-up routine: \"Final check\" in about 85%, \"Ready to …\" in about 45–50%, \"Final answer\" in 92–98%, and the reference answer in 92–94%. Cut-and-looped samples mostly never reach it: \"Final check\" appears in only 22% (GSM8K) and 8% (MATH). Yet 73% of the looped GSM8K samples already contain the reference answer before onset, and 47–65% have said \"final answer\"/\"answer is\". So most residual loops start in a \"verify again\" phase after the answer exists, and the model fails to move into its wrap-up.\n\nTo see what this transition looks like, I'll print two things:\n- In finished samples, the text just before \"Final check\" (how the model enters wrap-up).\n- In looped GSM8K samples, the text right after their last \"final answer\"/\"answer is\" before onset (what they do instead).\n\nIf the looped samples show a recognisable alternative at the same kind of line start (e.g., \"Let's try another interpretation\"), that line-start choice is the decision to study next.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: at the post-answer line start, finished runs enter wrap-up ('Final check') while looping runs open a new re-check. Inspect both.\ndef excerpt(ids, a, b): return asc(tok.decode(ids[max(0,a):b])).replace('\\n','|')\nrandom.seed(3)\nprint(\"=== FINISHED x2: context before first 'Final check' ===\")\nfor k in random.sample(finK, 5):\n    t = tok.decode(IDS11[k]); m = re.search(r\"Final [Cc]heck\", t)\n    if m: print(f\"[{k[0]}] pos {m.start()}/{len(t)} chars: ...{asc(t[max(0,m.start()-200):m.start()+60]).replace(chr(10),'|')}\")\nprint(\"=== LOOP x2 gsm8k: after last 'answer is'/'Final answer' before onset ===\")\ngl=[k for k in cutL if k[0].startswith('gsm8k')]\nfor k in random.sample(gl, 6):\n    on=int(LI11[k]['onset']); t = tok.decode(IDS11[k][:on]); ms=list(re.finditer(r\"answer is|[Ff]inal [Aa]nswer\", t))\n    if ms:\n        m=ms[-1]; print(f\"[{k[0]}] last@{m.start()} of {len(t)} chars (onset tok {on}) ref={ans_of[k[0]]}: {asc(t[max(0,m.start()-80):m.start()+200]).replace(chr(10),'|')}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7051,"cache_read_input_tokens":40162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7051},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50029033-f34d-4508-b774-d69c349ab91f","uuid":"53f3a191-6cc7-4ba9-96b3-f4907b364f4d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T07:22:08.899Z","request_id":"req_011Cgtqtkm5SMC7xGKxqmumz"}
